### Description

### Problem

When the default value of a date input is empty, calling `control.reset()` (which can be called directly or by a parent) does not clear invalid text.

This may be a dupe of #33610 which was closed due to inactivity

### Potential Cause

Looks like this may have introduced by a change in the `writeValue` function on `MatDatepickerInputBase`

The below will no longer format the input field if the control value is currently empty and the input has invalid text.

```typescript

  writeValue(value: D): void {
    // We produce a different date object on each keystroke which can cause signal forms'
    // interop logic to keep calling `writeValue` with the same value as the user is typing.
    // Skip such cases since they can prevent the user from typing (see #32442 and #32475).
    this._assignValueProgrammatically(value, value !== this.value);
  }

  protected _assignValueProgrammatically(value: D | null, reformat: boolean) {
    value = this._dateAdapter.deserialize(value);
    this._lastValueValid = this._isValidValue(value);
    value = this._dateAdapter.getValidDateOrNull(value);
    this._assignValue(value);

    // date adapter turns invalid dates to null so `reformat` from `writeValue` is false
    if (reformat) {
      this._formatValue(value);
    }
  }  
```

In previous versions, `_formatValue` would always be called.

### Reproduction

StackBlitz link: https://stackblitz.com/edit/1hicipgd

Steps to reproduce:
1. Enter in any invalid date text into the field tied to a form control
2. Call `control.reset()`  (`Reset Datepicker` button in StackBlitz)

### Expected Behavior

Control should reset to default value (empty in this case) and the invalid input text should be cleared

### Actual Behavior

Invalid value text remains in the input

### Environment

- Angular: 22.2.0
- CDK/Material: 22.2.0
- Browser(s): Chrome 155.0.8059.85 
- Operating System: Windows

